  "query_preview": "/Wednesday through Sunday/...\nAs the Desert Southwest upper-level ridge builds Wednesday, \ntemperatures will be near normal under dry conditions. Starting \nThursday, flow aloft will be shifting from southwesterly to \nsoutherly as a Pacific low pressure system moves closer to shore. \nThis will increase precipitation chances Thursday and further \nFriday, primarily over higher terrain. Temperatures will become hot \nThursday and Friday under this pattern. Late Friday into the \nweekend, the trough will move onshore and then northeast across the \nPacific Northwest states. Showers and thunderstorm chances will \npersevere as the trough enhances large-scale lift and carries \nmoisture. Several degrees of cooling will be likely for Saturday and \nSunday.",
